# Vue 3 Dashboard Standards

This is an interview take-home. Code must look like a careful human wrote it — not bulk AI output.

## Composition API only

- Always `<script setup lang="ts">`
- Never Options API (`data`, `methods`, `computed: {}` in export default)
- Pinia: setup stores (`defineStore('id', () => { ... })`) with `ref` / `computed`
- Prefer `computed` over `watch`
- Thin components: templates + store calls + display formatting only

```vue
<!-- ✅ -->
<script setup lang="ts">
import { storeToRefs } from 'pinia'
import { useSalesStore } from '../stores/salesStore'

const store = useSalesStore()
const { summaryStats } = storeToRefs(store)
</script>
```

## Project layering

| Layer | Put here | Not here |
|-------|----------|----------|
| `types/` | types, constants | logic |
| `utils/` | pure transforms | Vue/Pinia imports |
| `stores/` | shared state + actions | chart config, CSS |
| `composables/` | chart-ready datasets | raw filter math (use utils) |
| `components/` | UI | business calculations |

## Comments — write like a person

- Few comments. Only where intent is not obvious.
- Casual / short. Not tutorial or architecture essays.
- No phase markers, no "AI generated", no `Populated in Phase X`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
// This function filters sales records based on the selected categories and months
// to ensure reactive updates across the dashboard components.

// ✅ GOOD
// start after end? just return empty
// toggle off if they click the same bar again
```

## Avoid AI-looking code

- Prefer small components over one fat file (e.g. FilterBar → DateRangeFilter + CategoryFilter)
- No dead code, unused imports, placeholder TODOs left in shipping UI
- No over-abstraction (factories, unnecessary wrappers)
- No purple-gradient / glassmorphism / emoji-heavy UI
- Prefer Tailwind utilities already in the project; keep layout simple
- Name things clearly: `filteredRecords`, `setDatePreset` — not `data`, `handleClick1`

## TypeScript

- Explicit types on public functions and store state
- No `any`
- Handle empty filters (`hasFilteredData`) instead of broken charts

## Security

- No `v-html` with user/mock content
- No secrets in frontend
